<b>Chirpy, chirpy, chirpy...</b>

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:00.210
<b>Chirpy, chirpy, chirpy...</b>

00:08:59.170 --> 00:08:59.830
<b>Chirpy, chirpy, chirpy...</b>

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:00.670
<b>Chirpy, chirpy, chirpy...</b>

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:00.670
<b>Chirpy, chirpy, chirpy...</b>

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:00.670
<b>Chirpy, chirpy, chirpy...</b>

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:00.670
<b>Chirpy, chirpy, chirpy...</b>

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:00.670
<b>Chirpy, chirpy, chirpy...</b>

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:02.960
Shamiko...

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:07.420
Am I just supposed to have a sleepover at school
until you come back in September?

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:10.670
Don't give up, Shamiko! It can be a little embarrassing
to fetch something that you forgot from school

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:12.710
after the closing ceremony is over.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:30.250
<b>BANDA TERRACE</b>

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:27.710
It's supposed to be around here somewhere.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:30.250
Tama City, Sakuragaoka block 3...

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.710
Huh? What are you doing out here, Mikan?

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.330
Oh, Shamiko! What perfect timing!

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:38.000
I'm searching for an apartment complex that's nearby.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.880
<b>STUMPED</b>

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.880
<b>STUMPED</b>

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.880
<b>MIKAN IN</b>

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.880
<b>TROUBLE</b>

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:40.880
It's called the "Banda Terrace."

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:46.880
<b>BANDA TERRACE</b>

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:43.460
But all I see at the address are abandoned ruins.

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:45.630
Uh, that's actually where I live.

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:46.880
See? This is Banda Terrace.

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:49.380
Guess it just looked like ruins to you, huh?

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:50.170
No!

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:54.040
I think it's a building with an incredibly retro feel
that you just don't see very often these days!

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:55.080
Sluuuump...

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:55.290
<b>Sluuuump...</b>

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:58.790
<b>BANDA TERRACE</b>

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:58.250
BaNdA TeRrAcE...

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:00.460
So, you're moving in?

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:04.540
Yeah. But I had no idea I would be living
in the same apartment complex that you do, Shamiko.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:08.460
Wait, I thought that high schoolers
couldn't rent apartments all by themselves...

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:09.250
It's okay!

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:12.670
This is actually a special property where people
related to the Light and Dark Clans can live

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:16.250
without going through any sort
of complicated approval process.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.830
See? I've got the keys.

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:17.880
<b>THE KEYS</b>

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:21.540
Plus... we offer a light-or-dark discount
on this particular unit for 120 yen a month!

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:22.170
Whoa!

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:24.290
And how could I possibly say no to that!

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:26.080
They reduce the rent like its some student discount?!

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:30.080
Gosh, this town really is strange.

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:31.130
That's for sure.

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:34.960
Momo said that it was developed as an easy place
to live back during the time Ms. Sakura was active.

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:39.540
That reminds me, I'm sorry I got all bent out of shape
when talking about her the other day.

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:43.880
I know that I made a big mess of your clothes
because of my curse.

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.040
Oh, something like that did happen.

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:47.540
Just look at how I ended up!

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.420
Would you care to pick out some of my clothes?

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:50.330
Can I really?!

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:52.880
I was planning to cut down on them
after my move, anyway.

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:58.540
Do you happen to have any
that don't expose the shoulders?

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:00.000
Sorry, but all of mine are like that.

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:05.380
Wasn't it Momo who asked you
to come to this town in the first place?

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:07.250
You could've just kept staying with her.

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:08.250
True.

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:11.040
But the problem is there are some things
I'd like to think about alone.

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:13.960
Did you get into a fight with Momo or something?

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:16.330
No, I wouldn't really put it that way...

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:23.330
<b>BABADUM BADUM</b>

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:23.330
<b>BADUUUUM</b>

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:23.330
<b>BABADUM BADUM</b>

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:23.330
<b>BADUUUUM</b>

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:23.210
Babadum badum baduuuum. Babadum badum, baduuuum.

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:20.130
But Momo always gets up early
and makes a big racket with her weird training.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:21.130
"Weird training"?!

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:23.210
We just operate on totally different schedules.

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:27.210
The truth is I owe somewhat of a debt
to both Ms. Sakura and Momo.

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:31.580
When I was younger,
my curse was a lot worse than it is now.

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:34.380
Ms. Sakura used her magic to restrain some of its power,

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:37.380
which is what enabled me
to actually interact with other people.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:41.670
Interfering with a curse, eh?
Sounds similar to what happened with Shamiko.

00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:44.080
What kind of person is Sakura Chiyoda actually like?

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:46.420
Very pretty and very strong, but a little careless.

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:49.880
Honestly, I'm not too worried
about the fact that she's gone missing.

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:51.170
She's gotta be alive somewhere.

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:52.130
SHOCK!

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:55.880
So, she's not the type to force innocent demons to dance
or fling them out the window with all her might?

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:54.580
Dance! Dance!

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:55.880
Fling!

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:59.460
I don't think she'd ever do that!
Why would you ask me such an oddly specific question?

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:03.250
Anyway, since I've found myself
a place to stay that's nice and cheap,

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:05.290
I'm gonna focus on doing my best!

00:12:06.670 --> 00:12:09.960
I'm a little disappointed at how old it is,
but if I just fix up the wallpaper...

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:12.830
<b>TALISMAN</b>

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:15.460
I knew something was wrong,

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:20.130
<b>Shudder</b>

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:20.130
<b>Shudder</b>

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:20.130
<b>Shudder</b>

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:20.130
<b>Shudder</b>

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:17.330
120 yen is way too cheap even with a discount!

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:18.540
Calm down, Mikan!

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:20.130
It's probably just some kinda stylish wallpaper!

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:27.250
I'm starting to think the brave face that Mikan puts on
is just an act, and she's always scared deep down.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:27.250
Gotta stay calm, gotta stay calm, gotta stay calm...

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:27.920
<b>COMPOSED</b>

00:12:27.460 --> 00:12:28.670
Oh, I know!

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:33.330
And yet she still came to this town to help me,
despite not knowing who I was.

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:33.830
Ah, nothing calms me down more than this.

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:35.380
Hey, Mikan?

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:39.380
Listen, I'm going to start searching
for a way to free you from that curse.

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:41.040
Consider it a housewarming gift for my new neighbor!

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:41.920
Shine!

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:45.920
What new neighbor? I'll have you know,
I'm escaping from these ruins as soon as possible!

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:47.790
They're not ruins! They're apartments that people live in!

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:50.580
Oh my. I'm hearing Yuko's voice
coming from somewhere.

00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:50.580
But for some reason I'm feeling a chill on my shoulders.

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:53.670
This room must have been cursed before I even got here.

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:51.710
Next door?

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:55.750
Mom! I think I hear Sis talking to somebody next door!

00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:55.750
No, it's because you don't cover your shoulders!

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.080
I wonder if someone new has moved in?

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:01.130
Will you consider helping me
accomplish my goals, Mikan?

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:02.460
In honor of our becoming neighbors!

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:03.420
"Goals"?

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:04.460
Yeah, I have a bunch!

00:13:04.460 --> 00:13:06.670
Here's a list. Number 1: Find Ms. Sakura.

00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:16.960
<b>1: FIND</b>

00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:16.960
<b> MS. SAKURA</b>

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:16.960
<b>2: FIND DEMONS</b>

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:16.960
<b>AROUND TOWN</b>

00:13:06.830 --> 00:13:08.540
Number 2: Find fellow demons around town.

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:16.960
<b>3. UNDO POWER</b>

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:16.960
<b>OF THE SEAL</b>

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:16.960
<b>PLACED ON</b>

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:16.960
<b>MY FAMILY  </b>

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:11.080
Number 3: Undo the power
of the seal placed on my family.

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:16.960
<b>4. DAD TURNED INTO A BOX</b>

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:16.960
<b>AND IT'S A BIG MYSTERY</b>

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:13.880
Number 4: My dad turned into a box somehow
and it's a big mystery that needs solving.

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:16.960
<b>THAT NEEDS SOLVING</b>

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:16.000
And last, number 5: I want to turn Momo into my vassal!

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:16.960
<b>5: TURN MOMO</b>

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:16.960
<b>INTO MY VASSAL</b>

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:16.960
Nod, nod.

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:20.000
I'm sorry, I'm seriously lost and have no idea
what you're talking about.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:22.580
Yeah, my head is spinning just from explaining it.

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:25.750
Listen up, Shamiko. Considering the situation,
I think your top priority should be

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:28.540
to search for leads
on the whereabouts of Sakura Chiyoda.

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:29.080
Huh?

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:33.920
From what I can tell, Sakura was the top dog responsible
for keeping the special environment of this area safe.

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:38.460
Once you find her and bring her back, then we can
all rest easy knowing the city will be more secure.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:39.960
While you're out looking for fellow demons,

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:42.630
keep your eyes open for evidence
that Sakura left behind.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.540
This super cheap and super ominous apartment complex

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:46.880
may be a remnant of something
Sakura set up in the past.

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:50.500
Oh God, I just knew this place was bad news.

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:52.330
<b>SPLOOOOSH!!</b>

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:51.630
Aw crap! I shouldn't have said that!

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:52.170
Ancestor!

00:13:56.880 --> 00:14:00.750
Sakura is a magical girl who specializes
in interfering with curses and barriers, right?

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:03.960
Plus, she had something to do
with sealing your father away in that box.

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:07.290
Just think about it, finding Sakura
will not only give us a huge power boost,

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:09.500
but also help us figure out
how to deal with the curses.

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:12.630
Furthermore, she can tell us everything
about what happened when your dad disappeared.

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:14.830
It'll advance so many of our goals all at the same time!

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:17.500
Like killing a whole flock of birds with one big stone!

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:20.380
Most importantly, Sakura is the type of person
who won't bully me!

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:24.460
If she steps in to take over for Momo as the boss
around here, it will leave me an opening to strike!

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.540
Oops! Did I start talking crazy?

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:27.750
You're amazing, Ancestor!

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:29.960
I'm really impressed! That was all so easy to understand!

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:30.790
Oh... good.

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:31.670
We should make her some offerings!

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:33.290
Great idea! I hope she doesn't mind mikan buns

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:36.210
That's weird. I totally ran my mouth off
and even sneered evilly, but I didn't get in any trouble...

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:34.080
because that's all I have.

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:38.710
<b>AMAZING</b>

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:38.710
<b>WOW</b>

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:38.710
<b>WOW</b>

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:38.710
<b>AMAZING</b>

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:39.290
Amazing! Amazing! Amazing!

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:40.130
What is this warm feeling in my heart?

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:42.460
I'm actually being useful and getting praised for once!

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:43.750
But it's not quite enough...

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:46.210
Lilith just opened a brand new door in life.

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:49.380
You should open up and tell Momo
exactly how you feel, Mikan!

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:52.830
You're right. I didn't really explain anything to her
before I left, so we need to have a talk.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:54.040
Whomp-whomp.

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:56.250
<b>PONDEROSA LEMON</b>

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:56.210
I was feeling as depressed as a ponderosa lemon earlier.

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:58.170
But now I'm on cloud nine!

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:01.790
Living on my own is full of new experiences
that are so much fun!

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:11.170
<b>FUFUFU...</b>

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:11.170
<b>HAHAHAHA</b>

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:11.170
<b>TEE HEE</b>

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:05.880
Oh boy, I just can't wait to set up a bookcase
and a TV in here!

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:09.380
And I'll bring a game console
so we can play against each other!

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:10.960
Gosh, that sounds like fun.

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:12.080
Momo?!

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:13.460
Gloooom...

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:13.580
<b>GLOOOOOOM...</b>

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:14.880
What do you think you're doing here?!

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:16.670
Because I wanted to get your advice.

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:20.540
I was rude when I barge into your house the other day
without introducing myself to your mom.

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:23.750
So I thought about bringing her a box of cakes
to formally say hello.

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:25.920
You don't have to worry about that.

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:30.880
But then I was worried it might be a terrible idea to bring
any sort of box, since your father is sealed in one...

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:33.210
You don't have to worry about that, either!

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:34.880
What do you think I should give her?

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:42.000
<b>BAM!!</b>

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:38.710
You really don't have to give us anything,
but I'll take a coupon for free rice if you're offering!

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:40.170
Mom?! What are you doing here?!

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:41.960
Because the walls are thin and I could hear everything!

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:46.290
Anyway, that's all from me. I said what I wanted to say,
so please continue your conversation.

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:47.210
Okay.

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:49.080
Gloooom...

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:52.830
I was concerned about Mikan after all that talk
about renting a room somewhere.

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:54.670
But it's nice to see you're doing just fine.

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:57.210
Huh? Momo? What's with that look?!

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:00.750
Aw, poor Momo. Are you feeling lonely?

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:02.330
Maybe a little abandoned?

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:03.000
Huh?

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:06.330
You're feeling down in the dumps because
Mikan and Shamiko are suddenly best buddies, right?

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:08.880
You and your mood are just so easy to read!

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:07.540
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:07.540
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:08.330
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:08.330
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:08.960
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:11.960
Go home and wallow in the sorrow
of a frozen meal heated in the microwave!

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:09.710
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:09.710
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:09.710 --> 00:16:10.540
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:09.710 --> 00:16:10.540
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:11.290
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:11.290
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:12.040
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:12.040
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:12.040
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:12.750
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:12.920
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:12.920
<b>BWHAHAHA</b>

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:14.330
Bye.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:17.080
<b>BYE</b>

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:15.630
Well, that figures!

00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:17.080
ANCESTOOOOR!

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:24.290
I'm not feeling lonely or anything,
but I'm going to stay here for summer vacation, too.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:24.960
Huh?!

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.920
Besides, I noticed another open room nearby.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.500
Wait, but...

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:28.540
<b>WHAAAAT?</b>

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:33.000
<b>Bow</b>

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:30.830
I hope that we can get along, Miss.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:32.290
Of course, the pleasure is all mine.

00:16:32.290 --> 00:16:33.000
Mom?!

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:42.130
<b>DOOM</b>

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:42.130
<b>DOOM</b>

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:42.130
<b>DOOM</b>

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:37.750
So I have to spend my entire summer vacation
living between two magical girls?!

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:38.920
Don't give up, Shamiko!

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:42.000
Become a demon who has
a harmonious relationship with the neighbors!

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:46.750
<b>BANDA TERRACE</b>

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:46.750
Allow me to properly introduce myself.

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:51.250
<b>HINATSUKI</b>

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:48.290
I'm Mikan Hinatsuki!

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:51.250
My family runs a citrus fruit
and processed food business.

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:55.580
Let me give you some of our yuzu dressing!
And some mikan cookies with sudachi juice!

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:57.580
That's very kind of you, thank you.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:17:00.580
Wow, Mikan, I didn't know your family
ran a food-processing plant!

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:02.880
We also produce a lot of things aside from food!

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.540
Whoa! Really?

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:11.130
<b>MIKANSY</b>

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:06.960
Check it out, this is some of our character merch.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.960
My dad actually made this based off one of my doodles!

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:10.960
How unique!

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.000
<b>THE AFTERNOON OF THE NEXT DAY</b>

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:13.670
Oh!

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:16.920
What's up, Momochiyo!
Did you come here to buy something?

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:23.330
<b>OMOIZAWA</b>

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:23.330
<b>WIENERS</b>

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:20.170
I'm trying to find a good gift to give to Shamiko's family.

00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:22.750
A gift, huh? Then why not some meat!

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:23.330
Uh, but...

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:26.130
We got really tasty beef here! You should give 'em some!

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:26.130
Wait.

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:28.880
They already mentioned wanting a coupon for free rice.

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:30.540
Come on, Momochiyo.

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:34.790
You know rice is only gonna become fat for Shamiko,
she needs this meat if she wants to build muscle!

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:37.000
Guess I'll get them some meat.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:41.380
<b>HYPE</b>

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:41.380
<b>HYPE</b>

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:41.380
<b>WOOP</b>

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:37.830
That's great!

00:17:37.330 --> 00:17:41.380
<b>WOOP</b>

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:39.170
You want to put it in a gift box?

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:41.210
No, please skip the box.

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:42.920
KAWHAAAAM!

00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:43.830
<b>KAWHAAAAM!</b>

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:43.630
Oh my gosh...

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:44.920
KAWHAAAAM!

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:45.500
<b>KAWHAAAAM!</b>

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:48.500
Is this really what I think it is? Oh my gosh!

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:49.540
It's meat.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:53.210
I'm going to be living next door to you for awhile,
so this is my way of saying hello.

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:55.750
Thank you for such a wonderful gift!

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:57.330
Yu! Ryo! Come on!

00:17:57.330 --> 00:17:58.330
KAWHAAAAM!

00:17:57.500 --> 00:17:58.670
<b>KAWHAAAAM!</b>

00:17:58.920 --> 00:17:59.540
<b>RED</b>

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:01.920
Guess what? Momo has blessed us
with the opportunity to gaze upon real beef!
Red! Red! Red! Red!<b></b>

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:00.420
<b>RED</b>

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:01.040
<b>RED</b>

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:05.290
<b>RED</b>

00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:02.630
Let's feast upon it with our eyes!

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:05.290
Hold on! I brought it because
I wanted you to cook it and eat it!

00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:05.790
Huh?

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:06.750
What the...?

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:08.380
KAWHAAAAM!

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:11.630
<b>KAWHAAAAM!</b>

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:11.630
Okay then, we're having a sukiyaki party tonight
to welcome our new neighbors!

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:14.630
We have plenty of ingredients inside
of our new refrigerator!

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:17.630
<b>RUMMAGE</b>

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:17.630
<b>RUMMAGE</b>

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:17.460
Are you sure you don't mind
having another mouth to feed?

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:19.750
No problem. Let's invite Mikan as well.

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:17.830
<b>SHUT</b>

00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:23.750
I can hear Daddy Box saying something to the effect
of "we should share with our neighbors."

00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:20.540
<b>GLINT</b>

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:25.080
Um, excuse me...

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.630
Maybe don't use the box
your husband is in to cut onions...

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:32.790
<b>MIKAN</b>

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:30.630
You don't have to worry
because the Daddy Box is incredibly sturdy.

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:32.750
And it purifies all filth on it within 3 minutes!

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:35.130
Okay sure, but I've got a folding desk
that you can use instead!

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:37.670
Mom, let's just use Momo's desk for tonight.

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:40.000
The Daddy Box is just too small to seat 6 people!

00:18:40.210 --> 00:18:41.130
Shamiko...

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:43.960
She actually counted me
as part of the number! That's my Shamiko!

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:44.000
Yay!

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:45.830
In that case, I'll use a proper cutting board.

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:46.880
I'll help you get everything ready.

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:48.130
Me, too.

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:49.130
I appreciate it.

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:50.960
I'm gonna peel the carrots!

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:51.830
Then I'll just...

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:54.830
GLOOOOOP!

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:54.880
<b>GLOOOOOP!!</b>

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.750
Shamiko... I screwed up cracking the eggs open.

00:18:57.750 --> 00:18:59.250
How on Earth does that even happen?!

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:01.330
Momo? Are you feeling okay?!

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:06.540
Listen, Shamiko and Ryo.
I'm about to call Mikan over here.

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:09.880
I want you to be very cautious
about letting her help do any of the cooking, okay?

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:10.460
Huh?

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:13.460
Does Mikan also have a bad habit
of transforming ingredients like this?

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:17.130
Gloop. Gloop. Gloop.

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:15.630
Also, do you think these need to be cooked?

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:17.130
It looks like they're moving.

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:19.170
That's not really the problem. It's just...

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:22.000
There's a slight issue
when it comes to her sense of taste.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:23.380
She wants to add citrus fruits to everything.

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:25.290
Acidity is what you need when dealing with a cold!

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:27.920
No matter the time or place,
she tries to make all foods more sour.

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:31.830
I understand that she has good intentions, but if
we're having sukiyaki then I want it to taste salty-sweet.

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:33.460
Because I think that goes better with rice.

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:34.830
Uh, okay.

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:34.830
I'm here!

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:35.670
Oh?

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:38.080
I see that Momo brought beef for tonight.

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:40.040
That's perfect since I have some lemons with me...

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:42.290
Hey, Ryo. Go out with Mikan to fetch some supplies.

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:43.670
KAWHAAAAM!

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:43.790
<b>KAWHAAAAM!</b>

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:48.750
This supermarket is just like it used to be.
Brings back memories.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.920
Does that mean you used to live in this town, Mikan?

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:52.630
Yes.

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:56.000
When I was young, one of my family's
factories was near here.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:58.710
But it was destroyed in an accident
and I ended up moving away.

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:03.710
I owe a lot to Momo and her big sister
because they really helped me back then.

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:05.210
I didn't know that.

00:20:05.580 --> 00:20:06.710
Hey, Mikan...

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:09.250
I think we need to buy more than citrus fruits.

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:11.130
I'm sorry! Bad habit!

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:14.460
Yuko. Be a dear and arrange the food on plates
with Momo, would you?

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:15.170
Okay.

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:17.670
Plating the food... plating the food...

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:19.880
Hold up! Why the heck did you transform?!

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:22.080
The eggs were ruined because of me.

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:24.500
So I'm going to use everything I have
to make this a success!

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:25.670
Calm down, Momo!

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:27.210
The food is starting to glow!

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:32.420
Well, Momo. After carefully observing you
for an extended period of time,

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:34.710
I've discovered that you do have one major weakness.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:38.460
You try way too hard to make sure
that everything goes perfectly all by yourself!

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:42.330
You need to have more trust
in other people on a fundamental level.

00:20:42.330 --> 00:20:44.040
Otherwise, a demon's gonna
take advantage of that someday!

00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:46.380
Are you sure you want to tell
your mortal enemy about her weakness?

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:48.580
Not really, but I owe you for giving us this meat!

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:49.790
Here's an offering.

00:20:50.130 --> 00:20:51.790
Wonderful! Thank you, Ryoko.

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:54.670
Good thing I found you hanging from the tree next door.

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:57.130
That might have been what Momo was aiming for!

00:20:57.130 --> 00:20:58.630
Bubble, bubble, bubble, bubble!

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:00.040
Cheers!

00:21:01.750 --> 00:21:04.250
This is my first time eating sukiyaki with actual beef!

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:15.960
Shamiko?!

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:19.420
Sorry about that! I was just having a moment
because the flavor was out of this world!

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:24.630
Never thought I'd be sharing a toast
with my mortal enemy.

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:26.000
This feels weird.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:28.330
It feels a little awkward for me, too.

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:30.880
Since we're going to be neighbors for awhile,
You know, I think that might be even tastier<b>
</b>with some lemon juice in it!<b></b>

00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:32.500
please let me know if the noise bothers you.

00:21:31.210 --> 00:21:34.710
Uh, no thanks. Really, I'm good.

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:33.880
My family can be rambunctious.

00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:34.710
That's okay.

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:37.170
I don't mind it when things are lively.

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:39.380
Is that so? I'm glad to hear it!

00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:41.500
Attention everyone. Can you hear me?

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:51.130
<b>Attention everyone.</b>

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:51.130
<b>Can you hear me?</b>

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:44.500
The tofu and onions are ready for eating.
Please hurry and get your fill.

00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:51.130
<b>The tofu and onions</b>

00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:51.130
<b>are ready for eating.</b>

00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:51.130
<b>Please hurry and get your fill.</b>

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:47.330
I would like to hurry and partake in the udon noodles.

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:46.790
<b>I would like to hurry</b>

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:46.790
<b>and partake in</b>

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:46.790
<b>the udon noodles.</b>

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:48.210
Stop it.

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:51.080
I don't think I can handle you
talking directly into my brain like that.

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:52.210
Here!

00:21:52.210 --> 00:21:54.880
I seasoned and grilled the leftover beef
with some salt and lemon!

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:56.750
It's yummy.

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:57.580
I know, right?

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:02.540
We need to talk. I hear that you were telling everyone
to be careful since I like to put lemons on everything!

00:22:02.710 --> 00:22:05.290
You should tell me to my face
whenever you have problems like that.

00:22:05.580 --> 00:22:07.330
Have some more faith in me, okay?

00:22:08.830 --> 00:22:11.250
Peach juice tastes even better with some lemon in it!

00:22:11.710 --> 00:22:13.420
What's with that look?

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:15.830
I'm still gonna throw in lemons
when I'm absolutely sure it'll be tasty!

00:22:16.710 --> 00:22:18.670
Trust me, it's delicious!

00:22:18.670 --> 00:22:20.040
I kinda want to try it myself.

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:23.670
You know, Seiko. Young people these days
have the most awkward conversations, eh?

00:22:23.670 --> 00:22:25.710
I love this drink...

00:23:56.130 --> 00:24:11.040
<b>PREVIEW</b>

00:23:57.080 --> 00:24:00.380
I'm Yuko Yoshida. I'm a demon.
And beef sukiyaki is way too yummy!

00:24:00.380 --> 00:24:03.080
Shamiko! Since it's summer,
we need to build your muscles and your stamina!

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:06.250
Wah! Magical Girl Momo's tyranny
is going to continue even during summer vacation!

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:07.000
Mikan here.

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:11.040
<b>URBAN EXPLORATION! THE TROUBLED MIKAN AND THE EXCITED DEMON</b>

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:09.250
Oh? We have a lot of those boxes at my family's factory!

00:24:09.250 --> 00:24:10.880
Whoa! Look at all the Daddy Boxes!
